<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santa Ana, Manila</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Santa Ana is a district of the City of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pasig-river">Pasig River</a>. It occupies the site of the pre-colonial polity of Namayan, and excavations around its church have uncovered burials with Chinese trade ceramics. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franciscans">Franciscans</a> founded a mission there in 1578, and its church, completed in the early 18th century, is one of the oldest in Manila.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santa-ana-manila.jpg" alt="Santa Ana, Manila" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roel Balingit · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ph_fil_manila_santa_ana.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
